pr_comments:
@agners proposed I2C implementation is very HA-specific and can be seen as a 'DataUpdateCoordinator' for I2C device.

I can move all i2c code within existing mcp23017 component but decided to isolate it as I developed other custom components, sharing the same i2c bus and wanted to avoid code replication, multiple threads running the same code and share a common/generic bus locking mechanism for all devices, e.g. e.g. hts221/lps22hb/veml6075 humidity/pressure/uv sensors in https://github.com/jpcornil-git/core/tree/Arduino_MKR_ENV/homeassistant/components.

This architecture also allows multiple mcp23017 to be instantiated on the same bus without threading issues.

@gralin just done; moving forward, I'll probably move mine to a custom or hacs component to ease maintenance of people already using it today (current one way too slow for e.g. light switches on top of #31867)
Cheers
jpc

